        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1266">

                <pb facs="1013" n="897" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg897"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.2311.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Governor of
                        Texas</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-09-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 28, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Government of Mexico desires the permission of the Government of the United
                    States for a brigade of Mexican Federal troops, under the command of General
                    Blanquet, to enter American territory from Piedras Negras, Coahuila, in order to
                    proceed by rail to Del Rio and Marathon, whence they will reenter Mexico. This
                    Government proposes to stipulate that the Mexican troops go unarmed, their arms
                    being shipped as baggage, and will also cause a small detachment of American
                    troops to accompany them on the train as an escort. Before the issuance of
                    definite instructions, I have the honor to request that you telegraph me, in
                    accordance with the customary formality, the assurance that this course will be
                    entirely agreeable to the State of Texas.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
